# Normalise line endings so the packed artefact is byte-identical on every build
# platform.
#
# Why this exists: the release publisher pins an exact tarball SHA-256. Without
# this file, a checkout on a runner with core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows
# default, and the GitHub windows-latest default) converts LF to CRLF, and
# `npm pack` then packs those CRLF bytes. The same commit produced two different
# tarballs — 245 bytes apart across 15 text files, every byte of it a carriage
# return.
#
# `eol=lf` forces LF in the working tree on every platform, so the artefact a
# consumer receives does not depend on which machine built it.

# Everything text-like is normalised to LF in the repository and the worktree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.tgz binary
*.vsix binary
